        "end": 177,
        "description": "reported C observation; not an independent validation"
      },
      "text": "`borg_write_map(true)` (the `^z` map command, not in any suite): when the\n  file prompt is cancelled or the file cannot be opened, the file stays\n  NULL. `file_putf()` ignores a NULL file, but `file_put()` (the \"Swap\n  ...: NONE\" lines, with `borg_uses_swaps`) and the final `file_close()`\n  dereference it, so the game crashes."
    }
